course: dictionary
lesson: 6761
title: Openly: in plain sight
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Openly means in a way that everyone can see or hear, not in secret. It can also mean honestly, without hiding how you feel or what you think. The words around it leave clues. «The sob he had fought with so long refused to be beaten» tells you Mole was trying hard to hide his tears, so when he «cried freely and helplessly and openly», the word openly shows that he stopped hiding them.
explain: Test your meaning by putting it into the sentence. Does "cried in a way everyone could see, and did not hide it" still make sense? Yes, so openly fits. Freely is a helpful clue too, because it also means without holding back.
explain: Openly is an adverb, so it tells you how something is done. Look at the verb next to it. «Paul handled collected gifts openly» means everyone could see how the gifts were handled. When someone talks openly to a trusted adult, they say what is really going on and do not hide it.
fact: Openly means in a way that everyone can see or hear, not secretly.
fact: Openly also means honestly, without hiding your feelings or thoughts.
fact: «Talk openly» means talk honestly, without hiding anything.
fact: Openly is an adverb: it describes how an action is done, as in «openly admit» or «openly disagree».
fact: Slang: "highkey" (US, young people) means openly or very much.
exercise: «Paul handled collected gifts openly.» What does openly mean here? | Only in front of his friends | In a secret place, behind a closed door | Quickly and without any care | *In a way everyone could see
exercise: Mia says she will talk openly to her teacher about the problem. What does talk openly mean? | Whisper so no one can hear | Talk about the weather | *Talk honestly, without hiding how she feels | Talk only by writing a note
exercise: In «he openly admitted it», which word tells you how he admitted it? | *openly | he | it | admitted
test: Which word means the opposite of openly, when something is done in secret? | Quickly | Happily | *Secretly | Loudly
test: «He openly admitted it.» What does this mean? | *He owned up to it in front of everyone, without hiding it | He refused to admit it | He forgot to admit it | He admitted it in a whisper
exam: A friend says she wants to talk openly about her worries. What does that suggest? | She has no worries at all | She wants to keep them secret forever | *She wants to share them honestly, without hiding anything | She wants to talk about the weather
